  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If three vertices of a regular hexagon are chosen at random, then the chance that they form an equilateral triangle is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NdCX2",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sTykm",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HDUpo",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{10}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XPLxn",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Three vertices can be selected in ${ }^{6} \\mathrm{C}_{3}$ ways.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/YwWmXDaEV9LZX_I_avY1qkPu_rA3XsvxmHeX49ysZMc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe only equilateral triangles possible are $\\mathrm{A}_{1} \\mathrm{~A}_{3} \\mathrm{~A}_{5}$ and $\\mathrm{A}_{2} \\mathrm{~A}_{4} \\mathrm{~A}_{6}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{p}=\\frac{2}{{ }^{6} \\mathrm{C}_{3}}=\\frac{2}{20}=\\frac{1}{10}$",
    "image": null
  },
